triage:C2_QA1_REQ_C2_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C2-001" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "docs/plans/phase-c/sprint-c-2-consumer-sc-lint-full-profile.md:11" ;
 triage:issue "The sprint requirements list omits applicable NFR-RUN-0003, NFR-RUN-0004 and NFR-RUN-0008. Its custom generation/bootstrap integration and changed generated Rust are constrained by the standard-tool, less-code and source-length requirements even though the template must not vendor maintainer line-count policy." ;
 triage:action "Add the applicable constraints to this sprint's requirements list and retain the current narrow native-tool/policy exception. This does not make C2 the acceptance owner of root maintainer line-count checks." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

triage:C2_QA1_REQ_C2_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C2-002" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:40; tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:95; tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:125; tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:140; tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:151" ;
 triage:issue "The new required generation regression launches external setup/lint/upgrade/init/analyzer processes with subprocess.run and captured pipes, without an absolute failure budget or owned process-tree cleanup. A stalled tool, blocked build, or descendant retaining a captured pipe can keep the generation suite waiting indefinitely. Passing executions do not make these waits bounded." ;
 triage:action "Use the repository's bounded owned-process facility (or an equivalent demonstrated ownership design) for every new subprocess test path. Add a causal stalled/descendant-held-output negative proving failure is bounded and the whole owned tree is reclaimed. Do not fix this by retries, skips, serialization or simply enlarging a timeout." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

triage:C2_QA1_REQ_C2_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "REQ-C2-003" ;
 triage:severity "Blocking" ;
 triage:reviewer "req-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:33; tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:38; tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:104; tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py:160; template/.sc-lint/bootstrap.py:81; template/.sc-lint/bootstrap.py:184" ;
 triage:issue "The new install/upgrade test inherits ambient tool installation settings and does not put SC_LINT_INSTALL_DIR under its TemporaryDirectory. With no reusable installation, the bootstrap installs to the user's XDG_DATA_HOME/LOCALAPPDATA/default home sc-lint location; the test also runs upgrade there. The test therefore does not guarantee filesystem isolation or independent installation state for two simultaneous suites. Current cached-tool success is not proof of the fresh-install path's isolation." ;
 triage:action "Give this test an owned installation directory and any other writable tool/cache state beneath its temporary root, handling ambient SC_LINT_BIN deliberately. Prove the fresh-install and upgrade paths cannot write outside that root and independent suite instances do not share mutable installation state." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

