triage:C2_QA1_ARCH_C2_006 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "ARCH-C2-006" ;
 triage:severity "BLOCKING" ;
 triage:reviewer "arch-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py" ;
 triage:issue "The new command helper runs setup/lint/upgrade/init with subprocess.run and captured pipes but no deadline or owned-process-tree cleanup. Equivalent direct calls occur at95,125,140,151. A stalled tool or descendant retaining stdout can hold the required generation suite indefinitely; TemporaryDirectory cleanup does not own or reclaim those processes. This violates quality-policy.md59-64 test ownership/no-hang policy. The promoted template logger fixture has the same unbounded cleanup pattern at template/crates/daemon/src/observability_adapter_tests.rs126 and166: both Drop and the timeout branch call Child::wait after kill, outside their polling deadline." ;
 triage:action "Use the existing bounded owned-tree execution mechanism for every new external command/probe, retain causal failure observations and physical cleanup on errors/assertions, and add an owned stalled/pipe-holding negative proof. Do not fix with retries, skips or larger timeouts. Cover the generated logger fixture destructor/timeout paths as well as the Python regression command helper." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

