triage:C2_QA1_FTQ_C2_001 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C2-001" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py" ;
 triage:issue "Consumer profile tests wait indefinitely for command completion and captured pipe EOF, and their direct cargo_generate calls also enter an unbounded captured subprocess path. A hung analyzer/Cargo/plugin or surviving inherited pipe writer can stall the whole unit suite." ;
 triage:action "Run every externally executing test path, including generation, through the existing bounded owned-process runner with regular-file capture and physical descendant cleanup on timeout/error/assertion failure. Cover causal adversarial stall and cleanup without retries or longer correctness windows." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

triage:C2_QA1_FTQ_C2_002 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C2-002" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "tests/unit/generation/test_consumer_sc_lint_profile.py" ;
 triage:issue "The public setup/upgrade test copies ambient installation environment and can mutate or race the user/global sc-lint installation outside its TemporaryDirectory. It can also select an ambient binary instead of exercising an isolated fresh installation." ;
 triage:action "Put managed installation and writable cache/config state under the test-owned temporary root, handle SC_LINT_BIN deliberately, and prove independent instances plus external sentinels remain untouched. Do not serialize tests to hide the shared state." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

triage:C2_QA1_FTQ_C2_003 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C2-003" ;
 triage:severity "critical" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "template/crates/daemon/src/observability_adapter_tests.rs" ;
 triage:issue "The generated logger fixture bounds its initial poll but can hang indefinitely while trying to reap on timeout or Drop. A kill request is not physical-completion proof." ;
 triage:action "Keep ownership and use a bounded physical-reap loop within the original cleanup budget on success/error/timeout/panic. Add causal status-inspection/kill/reap failure coverage; no bare unbounded wait, retry or timeout padding." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

triage:C2_QA1_FTQ_C2_004 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C2-004" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "crates/sc-cron/tests/hook_environment/owned_child_unix.rs" ;
 triage:issue "Inspector spawn, wait or nonzero-status failure returns before the owned direct launcher is physically reaped. Drop retries the same failing stop and only sends start_kill, so returning a cleanup error can leave the child alive or unreaped." ;
 triage:action "Retain launcher identity and the original cleanup deadline on every inspector failure; perform bounded termination and physical reap before releasing ownership, with a causal injected inspector-failure assertion at the return boundary. Consume the common C5 repair when available." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

triage:C2_QA1_FTQ_C2_005 a triage:Finding ;
 triage:id "FTQ-C2-005" ;
 triage:severity "important" ;
 triage:reviewer "flaky-test-qa" ;
 triage:status "open" ;
 triage:reviewed_commit "e4f01c5d160be7025ad1a6e22dd97676940b1be1" ;
 triage:file "tests/integration/generation/owned_process.py" ;
 triage:issue "The inner Python Windows owner equates empty Job Object accounting with physical termination of all descendant process objects. That can return before a retained descendant handle is signaled and make the immediate completion witness fail intermittently. The outer Rust emergency cleanup cannot retroactively qualify the inner return boundary." ;
 triage:action "Consume the shared retained-process-identity Windows owner correction and observe physical completion for each owned identity plus direct launcher before reporting return. Keep the existing zero-wait BEFORE witness; do not compensate with observer waits." ;
 triage:verification_source "https://github.com/randlee/sc-runtime/pull/119#issuecomment-6662398454" .

triage:C2_QA1_FTQ_C2_006 a triage:Finding ;
